<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hadhrami Bedouin Legion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1939–1967</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hadhrami <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bedouin">Bedouin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a> was a British-officered force raised in 1939 in the Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden-protectorate">Aden Protectorate</a>, modelled on the Arab Legion of Transjordan. Recruited mainly from Bedouin tribes, it kept order in the Qu'aiti and Kathiri sultanates of Hadramawt, guarding roads, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/well">wells</a> and forts. It ceased to serve the sultans in 1967, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> took over Hadramawt and the sultanates fell.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hadhrami-bedouin-legion.jpg" alt="Hadhrami Bedouin Legion" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Mr. Ibrahem at Arabic Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:H.B.L.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
